  "paper_id": "eurosys-2023-silod-a-co-design-of-caching-and-scheduling-for-deep-lea-befa17b1",
  "title": "SiloD: A Co-design of Caching and Scheduling for Deep Learning Clusters",
  "abstract": "Deep learning training on cloud platforms usually follows the tradition of the separation of storage and computing. The training executes on a compute cluster equipped with GPUs/TPUs while reading data from a separate cluster hosting the storage service. To alleviate the potential bottleneck, a training cluster usually leverages its local storage as a cache to reduce the remote IO from the storage cluster. However, existing deep learning schedulers do not manage storage resources thus fail to consider the diverse caching effects across different training jobs. This could degrade scheduling quality significantly.",
  "abstract_source_id": "src-abstract-eurosys-2023-befa17b1",
